      "source": "",
      "text": "Concert Life and Music Performance\n\nAttending a live concert is a different experience from listening to recordings. The audience hears the sound directly from the stage and feels the energy of the performers. Many concert halls are designed for acoustic clarity so that every note reaches the listener. Festivals bring together artists and fans for several days of music. Ticket sales help to fund the events and pay the musicians. Rehearsals are essential before a performance so that the orchestra or band can coordinate tempo and dynamics. Conductors lead the ensemble and interpret the score. Soloists often perform concertos with orchestral accompaniment. Applause and encores are part of the tradition. Streaming services have changed how people discover and listen to music, but live performance remains important for both classical and popular music.\n",
